{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"externalID":"s:11Persistence12SegmentStoreV","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentStore"}],"modules":[{"name":"Persistence"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Persistence\/SegmentStore.swift#L57","fileName":"SegmentStore.swift"},"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SegmentStore","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","role":"symbol","title":"SegmentStore","symbolKind":"struct"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence"]]},"topicSections":[{"title":"Initializers","generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/init(events:directory:byteBound:segmentByteCount:)"]},{"title":"Instance Properties","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/byteCount","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/directory","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/pendingRecordCount"]},{"title":"Instance Methods","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/append(_:)","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/synchronize()","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/takeRecoveredRecords()"]},{"title":"Type Properties","generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/defaultByteBound","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/defaultDirectory"]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","doc:\/\/Persistence\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Persistence\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentStore"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let store = try SegmentStore(events: [SignedUp.self, CheckedOut.self])","let tracker = Tracker(store: store)","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: vendor)"]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Write-through.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" A tracker’s worker writes each record as it reaches it, before publishing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it, with one "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"write()"},{"type":"text","text":", off the tracking caller’s thread, so the record survives the app"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"crashing or being killed from then on. The store makes the log durable against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"power loss too ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fsync"},{"type":"text","text":") once per batch, before the batch is delivered, and whenever"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/synchronize()","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is called: call it, after the tracker’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush()"},{"type":"text","text":", as the app moves to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"background or terminates."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A record whose write fails (the disk is full, say) is kept in memory only, and reported as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/writeFailed(recordCount:timestamps:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"What is kept.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" Only events of the types in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"events"},{"type":"text","text":", which conform to "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/BinaryCodable"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Events of any other type are kept in memory only: they are delivered in this run like any"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other, are never written, and produce no drop report, but are lost if the app ends first."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A record’s context is not kept: a recovered record is in the top-level "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ServiceContext"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as its span ended with the earlier run."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Deleting.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" A segment is deleted as a whole once every record in it is delivered, so a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"log whose records are all delivered holds no files. There is no compaction: a segment kept"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for one undelivered record keeps its delivered ones too."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Bound.","type":"text"}]},{"text":" The log never holds more than ","type":"text"},{"code":"byteBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" bytes. When a record wouldn’t fit, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"oldest segments are deleted until it does, and each one deleted with records not yet","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delivered yields a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" on ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":". A record too large for an empty log","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is kept in memory only.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Recovery."}]},{"type":"text","text":" A store opened on a directory recovers the records earlier runs left there"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and a tracker given the store delivers them first. Each segment is cut at its first torn or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"corrupt record, keeping every intact record before it, and the bytes cut off are reported."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A segment comes back whole, delivered records and all. Each record a delivery had started on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"comes back with "},{"code":"isRedelivered","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" set, as it may have reached a destination already: one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delivered before the app ended, or one delivered just as it ended, before the store could"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delete its segment. A record whose delivery mark can’t be written is held back from that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delivery, so it is never sent twice unannounced, and delivered on a later launch."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Other versions."}]},{"type":"text","text":" A segment a newer release of the app wrote, in a later version of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"format, is left on disk untouched after a rollback, for that release to deliver: this one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"neither reads it nor counts it toward the bound. A segment in an earlier version, which this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one can’t read, is deleted and reported as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/corruption(byteCount:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Changed event types."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Each record’s event is a map of its properties by name, so a record","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"written before its type changed still reads: a property removed since is skipped, an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"optional one added since is ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and one with a default value added since has it. A record","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stored at another ","type":"text"},{"code":"Event.schemaVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" than its type’s now is dropped without being read and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reported as ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/versionMismatch(event:storedVersion:currentVersion:recordCount:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"One at the same version that can’t be read all the same, after a required property was added","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or a property’s type changed without raising the version, is dropped and reported as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/undecodable(recordCount:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Open one store per directory at a time; two would delete each other’s segments. Copies of a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"store share its log.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" that keeps records in a directory of append-only segment files, bounded in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"size, until they are delivered."}],"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/DropReport/corruption(byteCount:)":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/dropreport\/corruption(bytecount:)","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/corruption(byteCount:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Recovery found a torn or corrupt record, or a segment header it couldn’t read, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"discarded the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"byteCount"},{"type":"text","text":" bytes from there to the end of the segment."}],"fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"corruption","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"byteCount","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol","title":"DropReport.corruption(byteCount:)"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/defaultDirectory":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"defaultDirectory","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"FilePath","preciseIdentifier":"s:13SystemPackage8FilePathV","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/defaultdirectory","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/defaultDirectory","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where a store keeps its segments unless it is given a directory."}],"title":"defaultDirectory"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/append(_:)":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"append"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Events11EventRecordV","text":"EventRecord"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Events11EventRecordV","text":"EventRecord"}],"title":"append(_:)","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/append(_:)","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/append(_:)","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Writes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"record"},{"type":"text","text":" to the log before returning, when its event type is one of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"events"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it fits the bound."}]},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/defaultByteBound":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/defaultbytebound","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"defaultByteBound"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/defaultByteBound","title":"defaultByteBound","abstract":[{"text":"The bound a store has unless it is given another: 5 MiB (5,242,880 bytes).","type":"text"}]},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/persistence","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","kind":"symbol","title":"Persistence","abstract":[],"role":"collection"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/dropReports":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/dropreports","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A report of each drop, in the order they happen, from recovery onwards."}],"fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dropReports","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AsyncStream","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:ScS"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"DropReport","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11Persistence10DropReportO"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol","title":"dropReports"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/DropReport":{"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DropReport","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"DropReport","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/dropreport","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DropReport","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Records a store dropped before they were delivered, and why."}]},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/BinaryCodable":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/binarycodable","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/BinaryCodable","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BinaryCodable","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"BinaryCodable","abstract":[{"text":"A value with a compact binary form, CBOR (RFC 8949), that a store keeps on disk.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"BinaryCodable","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/takeRecoveredRecords()":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/takeRecoveredRecords()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"takeRecoveredRecords","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"EventRecord","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Events11EventRecordV"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/takerecoveredrecords()","title":"takeRecoveredRecords()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The records of the segments earlier runs left, oldest first, with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isRedelivered"},{"type":"text","text":" set on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each one a delivery had started on; later calls return none."}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/directory":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"directory"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"FilePath","preciseIdentifier":"s:13SystemPackage8FilePathV"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"directory","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/directory","abstract":[{"text":"Where the store keeps its segments.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/directory"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/BinaryCodable/init(from:)":{"url":"\/docu